<title>UK: CRICKET-RAIN WASHES OUT OPENING SESSION AT LORD'S.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-RAIN WASHES OUT OPENING SESSION AT LORD'S.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rain washed out the opening session of the first day's play in the second test between England and Australia at Lord's on Thursday.</p>
<p>The umpires had been due to make another inspection after the one p.m. (1200GMT) lunch interval but further showers prevented a start.</p>
<p>At two p.m. (1300GMT) the rain was still falling and the covers were on the pitch.</p>
</text>
